        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e8eec5c5-2d94-5c42-88fc-fca0bef8a209",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: First Battle of Kharkov, Operation Barbarossa, World War II\n- People: Wilhelm Keitel\n- Organizations: German 6th Army, Army Group South, Soviet Southwestern Front, Oberkommando der Wehrmacht\n- Places: Kharkov, Kharkiv, Ukrainian SSR, Nazi Germany\n- Roles: German field marshal, Chief of the Armed Forces High Command\n\nFacts:\n- Wilhelm Keitel was born on 22 September 1882.\n- Wilhelm Keitel was a German field marshal who served as Chief of the Armed Forces High Command, the Oberkommando der Wehrmacht, in Nazi Germany during World War II.\n- The 1st Battle of Kharkov was the 1941 tactical battle for the city of Kharkov, now Kharkiv, in the Ukrainian SSR during the final phase of Operation Barbarossa.\n- Wilhelm Keitel gave the name 1st Battle of Kharkov to that battle.\n- The 1st Battle of Kharkov was fought between the German 6th Army of Army Group South and the Soviet Southwestern Front.\n- Wilhelm Keitel died on 16 October 1946.",
